Client-ranked results, and the lifetime bug that blocks them.

Adds BM_FILTER_MODE_NONE, in which every item passes in the order the client
added it. beamenu ranks results itself (fuzzy match plus frecency), so bemenu's
substring filter would otherwise run second and throw that order away. The
filter string is still tracked and drawn, it just stops selecting.

bm_menu_filter() and bm_menu_get_filtered_items() both short-circuit for the
new mode. The short-circuit in bm_menu_filter() is load-bearing rather than an
optimisation: its old_filter memo returns early when the filter string has not
changed, which after a client repopulates the item list would leave the stale
filtered list in place.

Also fixes bm_menu_free_items(), which freed menu->filter_item and left the
pointer dangling. filter_item belongs to the menu's lifetime, not the item
list's: bm_menu_new() allocates it once and the BM_KEY_CUSTOM path writes
through it later. Any client that refills its item list, which one doing its
own ranking must do on every keystroke, would double-free it through the
following bm_menu_free(). It also used free() instead of bm_item_free(),
leaking the item's text.

diff --git a/lib/bemenu.h b/lib/bemenu.h
index b766c0a..6ff6531 100644
--- a/lib/bemenu.h
+++ b/lib/bemenu.h
@@ -167,6 +167,16 @@ BM_PUBLIC enum bm_priorty bm_renderer_get_priorty(const struct bm_renderer *rend
 enum bm_filter_mode {
     BM_FILTER_MODE_DMENU,
     BM_FILTER_MODE_DMENU_CASE_INSENSITIVE,
+    /**
+     * Every item passes, in the order the client added them.
+     *
+     * For clients that rank results themselves. The filter string is still
+     * tracked and drawn in the search row, it just stops selecting: the
+     * client reads it with bm_menu_get_filter(), decides what the list should
+     * contain, and repopulates the menu. Without this, a client-ranked list
+     * would be filtered a second time by substring and lose its ordering.
+     */
+    BM_FILTER_MODE_NONE,
     BM_FILTER_MODE_LAST
 };
 
diff --git a/lib/filter.c b/lib/filter.c
index 2b4e465..9472bbc 100644
--- a/lib/filter.c
+++ b/lib/filter.c
@@ -180,4 +180,39 @@ bm_filter_dmenu_case_insensitive(struct bm_menu *menu, bool addition, uint32_t *
     return filter_dmenu_fun(menu, addition, bm_strupstr, bm_strnupcmp, out_nmemb);
 }
 
+/**
+ * Filter that selects nothing, leaving every item in place.
+ *
+ * Used by BM_FILTER_MODE_NONE, for clients that rank results themselves.
+ * bm_menu_filter() short-circuits before reaching this, so it exists to keep
+ * the dispatch table total rather than to be called: a NULL entry there would
+ * be a loaded gun for whoever next adds a mode.
+ *
+ * @param menu bm_menu instance to filter.
+ * @param addition Unused; every item passes regardless of how the filter grew.
+ * @param out_nmemb uint32_t reference to filtered items count.
+ * @return Pointer to array of bm_item pointers, owned by the caller.
+ */
+struct bm_item**
+bm_filter_none(struct bm_menu *menu, bool addition, uint32_t *out_nmemb)
+{
+    (void)addition;
+    assert(menu && out_nmemb);
+
+    uint32_t count = 0;
+    struct bm_item **items = list_get_items(&menu->items, &count);
+
+    struct bm_item **filtered = calloc(count > 0 ? count : 1, sizeof(struct bm_item*));
+    if (!filtered) {
+        *out_nmemb = 0;
+        return NULL;
+    }
+
+    if (count > 0)
+        memcpy(filtered, items, sizeof(struct bm_item*) * count);
+
+    *out_nmemb = count;
+    return filtered;
+}
+
 /* vim: set ts=8 sw=4 tw=0 :*/
